^.*\.Rproj$
^\.Rproj\.user$
^_pkgdown\.yml$
^docs$
^pkgdown$
^\.github$
^results.*$
^README\.Rmd$
# The full GPL-3 text. GitHub detects the licence from a file named LICENSE, so
# it stays at that name in the repository -- but DESCRIPTION declares
# "License: GPL (>= 3)" without "+ file LICENSE", and a LICENSE file inside the
# tarball is then read as a licence stub that does not parse. Kept in the repo,
# out of the build.
^LICENSE$
^LICENSE\.md$
^\.Rhistory$
^cran-comments\.md$
^CRAN-SUBMISSION$
^codecov\.yml$
^\.lintr$
^benchmark$
# The full-resolution logo masters. They stay in the repository as the source of
# truth for the artwork, but shipping them would push the installed package over
# the 5 MB size threshold for an image nothing in the package reads. The 250 px
# man/figures/logo.png is the copy that ships, and is what the README and the
# pkgdown site use.
^logo$
# GitHub reads CITATION.cff from the REPOSITORY to render the "Cite this
# repository" box, never from the tarball, so shipping it gains nothing and
# R CMD check lists any unrecognised top-level file as a non-standard one.
# inst/CITATION is the copy that ships and is what citation("cyRAVEN") reads.
^CITATION\.cff$
# Docker build-context exclusions. Read by `docker build`, never by R, and
# R CMD check reports any hidden top-level file as probably included in error.
^\.dockerignore$
# The worked-example article and its 20 rendered figures. pkgdown builds articles
# from this source tree, so the published site carries them; the tarball does
# not, because self-contained HTML embeds every image and would add about 5 MB to
# the installed package for documentation nobody reads from an R session.
^vignettes/figures\.Rmd$
^vignettes/figures$
# Claude Code skill. Documentation for humans and agents, published through the
# pkgdown article rather than shipped in the tarball.
^\.claude$
# Maintainer working files (backlog, release procedure, draft commit messages)
# and the demonstration cohort from the README quick start, which is regenerated
# by inst/scripts/demo_data.R.
^dev$
^demo$
# The backlog. Untracked by git and not part of the package; listed here because
# R CMD build reads the working directory rather than git, and any unrecognised
# top-level file is reported by R CMD check as non-standard.
^ToDo\.md$
# The image prompt sheet is a working file for generating the documentation
# figures, not documentation itself. The images beside it are a separate
# question: they ship only if the vignettes that reference them ship, and that
# decision waits until they exist and their size is known.
^vignettes/images/prompts\.md$
# The concept illustrations. They are referenced by the vignettes and so are
# built into the site and the PDF manual, both of which are produced from this
# repository rather than from the tarball. Shipping them took the package from
# under a megabyte to 25 MB, five times CRAN's limit, for figures nobody reads
# from an R session. Every chunk that draws one is guarded with file.exists(), so
# a vignette built from the tarball renders without them rather than failing.
^vignettes/images$
